  "seoBody": "<p>A user is the person on the job, answering Checks on WhatsApp. They don't need an app, a login, or a laptop, just a phone with WhatsApp.</p><h2>Adding</h2><ol><li>Click <strong>Add</strong> on <strong>Contacts</strong>, on the dashboard.</li><li>Enter their name and mobile number (defaults to UK +44; use the picker for other countries).</li><li>Click <strong>Add</strong>. They receive a WhatsApp intro message.</li></ol><h2>What the user sees</h2><p>A normal WhatsApp chat. When you send a Check, they get something like:</p><p><strong>Quickler</strong><br>Hi Tom, Acme Gas has asked you to run the <em>Annual Safety Check</em> at 14 Station Road. Ready to start? Reply YES when you're on site.</p><p>Questions arrive one at a time. The user replies with text, numbers, photos, or voice notes. When finished, the report is generated and emailed to you.</p><h2>How the AI in Quickler works, and how to get the best from it</h2><p>A light switch is old-fashioned computer code. Press it and it does the same thing every time.</p><p>AI is more like a dice. Each time, it picks the most likely answer, so it is working on chances, not certainties. Every clear thing you tell it paints another side of the dice with the answer you want. A photo paints a side. \"Pin in, gauge in the green, in date\" paints three more. Paint five sides out of six and it is nearly always right, and a person has the last word to catch the sixth: nothing files until somebody says done, and anything Quickler cannot settle is raised for you rather than guessed.</p><p>It also works the other way. If the extinguisher is fine but you mention the broken one down the corridor, you have painted the wrong number. If you only say \"it's fine\", you have left the sides blank and it is guessing.</p><p>AI also cannot paint what it has never seen. Ask one about a book it has not read and it will not say \"I don't know\". It answers confidently from the reviews. Quickler knows only what you tell it in that room, plus your firm's Check. If you don't say it, Quickler cannot know it.</p><p>Being specific is what makes it work. Ask an AI to update \"John Smith\" and there are thousands of them. Say \"John Smith at Smith Cleaning in Perth, who I spoke to today\" and there is only one.</p><p>Quickler uses both the switch and the dice. Switches handle the things that must never be wrong, such as Yes, No or N/A only, and no question left unanswered. The dice handles the judgement: which box your words belong in.</p><p>Last, most inspection apps work like a lift. They stop at every floor in order, and you scroll from question to question. Quickler works more like a satnav. Walk into a room and say what you see in any order: floor, walls, call points, ceiling, lighting. It puts each thing in its place and asks only about what is still missing.</p><p><strong>In short: say what you see, be specific, and stick to what is in front of you.</strong></p><h2>Removing</h2><p>Click the cross next to their name. Checks already started finish, but no new ones can be sent. Historical data is kept so reports remain complete.</p><h2>How many people can I add?</h2><p>There is no limit on how many people you add, and no seat to buy. You pay only for the phone numbers doing checks: a number that did at least one check that month. Everyone else costs nothing, so add your whole team.</p><p>Still stuck? Email <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">hello@quickler.co</a>, we reply within one business day.</p>",
